# Functions over the 80-line limit, frozen 2026-09-15 when this repo turned the
# hub's --ratchets on. The gate then refuses GROWTH and NEW offenders only.
#
# Format: <path> | <function> | <lines> | <reason>
#
# Four-way contract: a new offender, growth, an unrecorded shrink and a stale
# entry all fail. Shrinking a function means updating its number here, and
# deleting the row once it drops under the limit -- that is what stops a baseline
# becoming cover for the next one.
# third_party/ANTfrastructure/docs/code-quality-tooling.md
#
# This is a QUEUE, not an accusation. Sixteen of the twenty-two rows are the
# benchmark port, and they carry the verdict pyproject.toml already records for
# their ruff codes: behaviour-frozen at import, split only behind tests.

